From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:18:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v20: use the generic Lineage AIDL fingerprint HAL

biometrics.fingerprint@2.0 was removed from hardware/interfaces. The
device was already using Lineage's generic HIDL service rather than one of
its own, and the AIDL replacement opens the same legacy libhardware
fingerprint_device_t through hw_get_module, so the vendor blob backing it
is unchanged.

persist.vendor.fingerprint.type is required: the service calls
UNIMPLEMENTED(FATAL) on a value it does not recognise, and an unset
property reaches that branch.
---
 v20.mk | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/v20.mk b/v20.mk
index 8ce32c0..97025d9 100644
--- a/v20.mk
+++ b/v20.mk
@@ -65,7 +65,12 @@ PRODUCT_PRODUCT_PROPERTIES += \
 
 # Fingerprint
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
-    android.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint@2.0-service
+    android.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint-service.lineage
+
+# The AIDL service aborts on an unset or unrecognised type, so this is not
+# optional. The V20's reader sits on the back below the camera.
+PRODUCT_VENDOR_PROPERTIES += \
+    persist.vendor.fingerprint.type=rear
 
 # IR
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
